{"name":"Thimble Red","hex":"#a05d8b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thimble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pitted, now usually metal, cup-shaped cap worn on the tip of a finger, which is used in sewing to push the needle through material.","As much as fills a thimble (sense 1); a thimbleful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To use a thimble (noun sense 1).","To sew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thimble"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thimble","blocks":[{"text":"A thimble is a small pitted cup worn on the finger that protects it from being pricked or poked by a needle while sewing. The Old English word þȳmel, the ancestor of thimble, is derived from Old English þūma, the ancestor of the English word thumb."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Fingerhut.jpg/330px-Fingerhut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thimble"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Fingerhueter-1568.png/330px-Fingerhueter-1568.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Fingerhueter-1568.png/330px-Fingerhueter-1568.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Der Fingerhüter (Thimblemaker) from Das Ständebuch by Jost Amman, 1568","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFingerhueter-1568.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Early_cylinder.jpg/120px-Early_cylinder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Early_cylinder.jpg/250px-Early_cylinder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Early_cylinder.jpg/120px-Early_cylinder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarly_cylinder.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/14c_Nurnberg_thimble.jpg/250px-14c_Nurnberg_thimble.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/14c_Nurnberg_thimble.jpg/500px-14c_Nurnberg_thimble.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/14c_Nurnberg_thimble.jpg/250px-14c_Nurnberg_thimble.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u